I agree with what you said about the Potion of loose intrinsic,
Boudewijn. I agree with "We addicts here...". But I don't agree 
with you're conclusion that there should be no potions of
enlightenment. Au contraire: I don't think a novice player can
conclude from this "You feel firm." that she got disint. resist.
But once she quaffed a PoE and saw what it did, maybe the idea
will come to her mind to quaff a PoE AFTER such a message...
But then, imo, the game has evolved in a way that NO novice
player really is able to win without being spoiled at times.
There should be much, much more hints: the quest leader should
give a hint how too go back to the dungeon (someone mentioned
this before, I don't recall his name, sorry); at some point in
the game should be made clear how to do this thing with the
candles, the candelab., bell, book and vibrating square;
it should be possible to get some information about artifacts,
named weapons...as it is, there's no way to figure out that
Excalibur protects from level drain (besides reading the
spoilers or the code...) etc.
For experienced players, nothing would change. For novice
players things would become a little less frustrating, without
really spoiling the fun.
Any comments?

